From a8b8cdde277205b3d39064ca786c9aa7ade4ca03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:02:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/encryption_info: free a list of init info without
 recursion

av_encryption_init_info_free() freed the next entry of the list by
calling itself, so freeing a list of N entries took N stack frames.
The mov demuxer builds such a list from every 'pssh' box of a file
(mov_read_pssh() appends one entry per box and frees the merged list
after storing it as side data), so a crafted MP4 with many small pssh
boxes exhausts the stack (CVE-2026-107678). FFmpeg master
(af25036ac091) still frees it recursively.

Free the entries in a loop instead, keeping the next pointer before
freeing each one. The frees are the same, in the same order for each
entry.

A crafted MP4 (one frame, 8000 pssh boxes of 32 bytes appended to its
moov) read by ffprobe with a 32, 64, 128 or 256 KiB stack: the
recursive free crashes with SIGSEGV, this one returns the duration.

What this leaves is a quadratic cost, not a memory-safety bug: for each
pssh box mov_read_pssh() parses the whole list back from the side data
and serialises it again. Measured with the same file and fewer boxes:
0.21 s for 1000 boxes, 0.77 s for 2000, 2.83 s for 4000 and 11.6 s for
8000 (a 256 KiB moov). The number of boxes is bounded by the size of
the moov, as FFmpeg bounds other entry counts by the size of the box
that holds them; no count limit is added here, because neither FFmpeg
nor the format defines one and any number would be invented. Removing
the quadratic cost needs the demuxer to keep the list and serialise it
once, which is left to FFmpeg.
---
 libavutil/encryption_info.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/encryption_info.c b/libavutil/encryption_info.c
index a3eb955d2de5..1412f5d7db33 100644
--- a/libavutil/encryption_info.c
+++ b/libavutil/encryption_info.c
@@ -219,15 +219,16 @@ AVEncryptionInitInfo *av_encryption_init_info_alloc(
 void av_encryption_init_info_free(AVEncryptionInitInfo *info)
 {
     uint32_t i;
-    if (info) {
+    while (info) {
+        AVEncryptionInitInfo *next = info->next;
         for (i = 0; i < info->num_key_ids; i++) {
             av_free(info->key_ids[i]);
         }
-        av_encryption_init_info_free(info->next);
         av_free(info->system_id);
         av_free(info->key_ids);
         av_free(info->data);
         av_free(info);
+        info = next;
     }
 }
 
